<title>NEW ZEALAND: Ergo/AMP drop fixed 2, 3 year rates to 8.45 pct.</title>
<headline>Ergo/AMP drop fixed 2, 3 year rates to 8.45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMP and its subsidiary Ergo on Friday dropped their two and three year fixed residential mortgage rates to 8.45 percent from 8.75 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Today's new rates are Ergo's lowest ever and emphasise the real savings the AMP Group is delivering to New Zealanders,&quot; said Graham Meyer, managing director of Ergo.</p>
<p>&quot;At a time when most lenders are playing catch-up to our last move, we can pioneer a new market low because of our more cost-efficient operation and the financial security of the AMP Group.&quot;</p>
<p>The new fixed rates are available from Monday.  </p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
